Z||000000||sdm1964||03-31-2000||08:58 PM||||I just bought an 86 fiero SE, I ran the vin on a decoder, 86 se notchback SPECIAL? The lady i bought it from bought it new, The question i have is did SE's come with a GT nose? She swears that she ordered it that way from the factory, GT nose and v-6. I was under the impression that se's have the iron duck and a regular nose.<BR>TIA, stephen||||reg||14
Z||000001||AL||03-31-2000||09:00 PM||||the 86 models also carried a v6 and nose,congrats on your car and enjoy the v6||||reg||14
Z||000002||sdm1964||03-31-2000||09:25 PM||||It has a blown head gasget and needs some love, new nose, drivers fender, headliner, etc. it was cheap and i couldn't turn it down. You know what i will be doing on the weekends!!!!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||03-31-2000||09:50 PM||||Hey!! I thought you said your next Fiero would be a GT.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Good find,<BR>Roy||||reg||1
Z||000004||sdm1964||03-31-2000||11:21 PM||||Yea that is what i said. The paper said GT but got to the ladys house and for $450.00 I just couldn't say no. I guess i will bring it back from the dead and trade or sell it for a fastback, Of course after all this work I would be insane to get rid of it, Guess i will own 2 notchbacks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> One white and one gold||||reg||14
Z||000005||lowCG||03-31-2000||11:42 PM||||My old car was an '86 4cyl S/E,had the nose,and something I've never seen before on a 4cyl.;Quad megafone,exhaust,usually seen on V6 cars.<BR>Sounds like a good find.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||04-01-2000||12:07 AM||||The 86 SE looks exactly like an 85 GT. Notchback with aero nose. The 84 and 85 SE's had the coupe front end. The 86 SE had the 4cyl as the base engine and the V-6 was an option. The rattle could be the sunroof latch or a loose screw in the third brake light. Sounds like a very good buy for that price! congrats!||||reg||1
Z||000007||sdm1964||04-01-2000||12:09 AM||||The vin check came back with a v-6, will be checking #,s when i drop the engine. It was the GT nose that really threw me off. I just always thought the came with a stock fiero nose. The body is the same as my 85 GT just labeled as an SE. Was really looking for a fastback but they think they are made of gold in Georgia. Guess i will be a notchback man.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||04-01-2000||12:43 AM||||As far as I know....<P>all 85-87 SE's have the GT nose and trim, not sure about the tail. They could have either motor. The SE with the GT nose & trim may only have been an option. I'm not sure, but I have seen them this way.<P>The 84-86 SC's have 4 cyl and the regular nose, notch back, and the ugly grooved moulding.<P>the 87-88 base, SC, and Formula all are notch back and the new style nose with round trim. All 88's are dual exhaust.<P>You can check the RPO codes to be sure. (Sticker by brake master cyl.) Anyone with Alldata can look it up for you. (You might want to offer a couple bucks for their trouble. Full Alldata subscriptions are not cheap.)<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||04-01-2000||12:50 AM||||The 86 and 87 SE's have the ribbed molding. The 85 SE was the coupe body style. <BR>||||reg||1
